{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> In my opinion this passage is joined with what precedes it, for the firmament was not made until the earth was dry, and the proof is \"on the day that YHWH Elohim made earth and heavens\" (Genesis 2:4) — and they were made on day one. For to see a hidden thing and for the gathering of what is scattered is not [an act of] creation. And so is its meaning: \"and Elohim had already said, let the waters be gathered,\" and there are hundreds like it in the Torah. Now, in the portion of Genesis I give you two witnesses: the first — \"and He placed there the man whom He had formed\" (Genesis 2:5), and afterward \"and YHWH Elohim caused to grow\" (ibid. 2:9), yet before the man He had already caused them to grow. And the second witness — He commanded the man not to eat of the tree of knowledge, and after it is written \"and YHWH Elohim formed from the ground\" (ibid. 2:19), only its meaning is 'and He had already formed.' And on this interpretation \"and Elohim saw that it was good\" is joined with the creation of the second day, and 'let the earth bring forth vegetation' [belongs to] the beginning of the third day." "And the meaning of יקוו is 'let them be gathered,' as in ונקוו אליה (Jeremiah 3:17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase הראות דבר נסתר והקוות מפוזר is translated hyper-literally; the construction is compressed and the syntax is difficult, possibly reflecting a textual difficulty in the witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:34.249654616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}